1525..1596 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1597..1670 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1671..1748 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1749..1815 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `Path.step(loop ∷ p, q)` is"
1816..1892 Comment "/// `loop ∷ Path.step(p, q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1893..1960 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first; the"
1961..2025 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions."
