2292..2369 Comment "/// Winding a composite is summing the windings (cubical\'s `winding-hom`), by"
2370..2444 Comment "/// induction on the first loop, written last so its match stands directly"
2445..2523 Comment "/// under the recursion, where the checkers read it as a fold, and summed with"
2524..2588 Comment "/// `wind(q)` first because the sum descends its second summand:"
2589..2669 Comment "/// `Path.here(wind(q))` on the empty word, and the recursive call carried along"
2670..2743 Comment "/// `up` or `down`. The composite in its type is read off the parameters\'"
2744..2796 Comment "/// written types, and the kernel reads its endpoint"
2797..2849 Comment "/// `plus(wind(q), wind(p))` as the call it returns."
